Modelica source:
```modelica
connector HeatPort
  Real T;
  flow Real Q_flow;
end HeatPort;
model Capacity
  HeatPort port;
end Capacity;
model Convection
  HeatPort solid;
  HeatPort fluid;
end Convection;
model Study
  HeatPort boundary;
  Capacity core;
  Capacity Tcore;
  Convection convection;
equation
  connect(boundary, core.port);
  connect(core.port, Tcore.port);
  connect(Tcore.port, convection.solid);
end Study;
```

Question:
Within the equation scope of model instance Study, return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set formed by explicit connect statements in that scope that contains boundary.Q_flow.

Target:
boundary.Q_flow

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
Return exactly {"answer":"..."}.
